    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0473" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg377"/>

                <head>No. 282.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 27, 1872</date>.
                        (Received February 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 504.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send herewith a copy
                    and synopsis (A and B) of a notable article upon “Cattle-stealing on the
                    Frontier,” written by Don Emilio Velasco, and published on the 4th instant in
                    the Siglo XIX, of which paper he is one of the editors. The author was a
                    prominent member of the last congress, representing the northern district of
                    Tamaulipas, which is that of the Texan frontier, and he was formerly secretary
                    of the government of that State. He belongs to the Lerdista party, and
                    consequently his opinions and suggestions regarding the conduct of the Mexican
                    government in this matter are entitled to considerable weight.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d282-a1.xml" xpointer="d282-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
